LISA async_copy_source_written_before_the_wait
(* A copy engine reads the source of raw::async_copy until raw::async_wait (C6). A lane that
   writes the source before the wait races with the engine. P0 is the lane: the release of go
   starts the copy. P1 is the copy engine.
   Expect: sometimes, a data race. *)
{ src = 1; dst = 0; go = 0; done = 0; }
 P0                  | P1                   ;
 w[rel] go 1         | r[acq] r0 go         ;
 w[plain] src 2      | r[plain] r1 src      ;
                     | w[plain] dst r1      ;
                     | w[rel] done 1        ;
scopes: (device (block P0) (block P1))
filter (1:r0 = 1)
exists (1:r1 = 2)
